<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Codecov: Edit and validate codecov.yml" id="Codecov-Usage">

    <primary-label ref="codecov"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Validate: right-click <path>codecov.yml</path> and select <control>Validate Codecov YAML</control></p>
        <p>Setting: <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov</ui-path>, <control>Inject codecov YAML schema</control></p>
        <p>Validation requires: a Codecov API token in the plugin settings</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Get code completion and documentation for codecov.yml, and validate the file against the Codecov server.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Get completion for codecov.yml and validate it against the Codecov server.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>The Codecov plugin adds completion, quick documentation and server-side validation for codecov.yml files to JetBrains IDEs, before you commit.</web-summary>

    <p>
        The plugin bundles the Codecov YAML schema, so the editor helps you write the Codecov configuration file.
        Before you commit, you can let the Codecov server check the file.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Edit codecov.yml with completion" id="config-file">
        <p>
            The schema applies to every <path>.yml</path> or <path>.yaml</path> file whose name contains <code>codecov</code>, such as <path>codecov.yml</path> and <path>.codecov.yml</path>.
            In these files, the editor offers:
        </p>
        <list>
            <li>Code completion for keys and values.</li>
            <li>Quick documentation for keys.</li>
            <li>Highlighting of unknown keys and wrong value types.</li>
        </list>
        <!-- planned-image src="codecov_yaml_completion.png" alt="Code completion for Codecov YAML keys" -->
        <p>
            The status bar shows <control>Codecov Yaml</control> as the schema of the file, and the Project tool window and editor tabs show the Codecov logo as its icon.
        </p>
        <p>
            The schema is on by default.
            To turn it off, clear <control>Inject codecov YAML schema</control> in <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov</ui-path>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Validate codecov.yml" id="validate-codecov-yml">
        <p>
            Validation sends the content of the file to the Codecov server set in <control>Server URL</control> and reports the result.
            It is offered for files named exactly <path>codecov.yml</path> or <path>codecov.yaml</path> while <control>Inject codecov YAML schema</control> is on.
            It needs the API token that you set when you <a href="Codecov-Installation.topic" anchor="codecov-sign-in">connect the project</a>.
        </p>
        <procedure title="Validate the file" id="validate-config">
            <step>
                Save the file (<shortcut>Ctrl+S</shortcut>, macOS: <shortcut>⌘ S</shortcut>).
                Validation sends the saved content of the file, not unsaved changes in the editor.
            </step>
            <step>
                Right-click <path>codecov.yml</path> in the Project tool window, or right-click in the editor of the open file.
            </step>
            <step>
                Select <control>Validate Codecov YAML</control>.
                <!-- planned-image src="codecov_validate_menu.png" alt="Validate Codecov YAML in the Project tool window context menu" -->
                A notification reports "Codecov configuration is valid." or "Codecov configuration is invalid." and names the file.
                <!-- planned-image src="codecov_validation_result.png" alt="Notification that the Codecov configuration is valid, with View Validation Results" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                Optional: click <control>View Validation Results</control> to open the full server response as a JSON file in the editor.
                <!-- planned-image src="codecov_validation_json.png" alt="Validation results opened in the editor" -->
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            If no API token is set, the warning "Codecov API token is missing. Please configure it in Settings." appears instead.
            If the server cannot be reached, the error starts with "Failed to validate codecov.yml:".
        </p>
    </chapter>

